 "drafts": [
  {
   "stage": "direct_draft",
   "passage": "On the Tamsin-News test split, Verisum reduced the hallucination rate from 15.1% (Corran-Sum) to 8.7%, a relative reduction of 42.4%, while the salience pre-filtering re-implementation alone reduced it to 11.0% (a 27.2% relative reduction). The 27.2% relative reduction from the salience filter is consistent with the approximately 31% reduction reported by Varga & Sandoval (2021) for salience pre-filtering across three news benchmarks. Verisum's additional reduction beyond the salience filter (from 11.0% to 8.7%, a 20.9% relative improvement) suggests that the entity-grounding loss contributes further to reducing unsupported entities, though no statistical tests were reported to assess the reliability of these differences.",
